The same retained InoriRus MIT grant and GPL-2.0-only port license apply.
PentaX additions upload actual linear RGBA8 target contents, LOAD them, draw
with the actual prepared compiler products, fence and read back every pixel,
and issue a core completion only after same-owner transactional writeback.
Stage push data is merged by manifest placement (normally VS dword 0 and PS
dword 16); conflicting live overlaps are refused. This first profile excludes
descriptor resources, interpolation, tiled/DCC targets, depth, blending, MSAA,
indexed draws and presentation. It does not replace the registered tiled-video
surface conversion or prove that any commercial title frame is presented.
Vulkan load/store, transfer and push-constant requirements are from:
https://docs.vulkan.org/spec/latest/chapters/renderpass.html
https://docs.vulkan.org/spec/latest/chapters/synchronization.html
https://docs.vulkan.org/refpages/latest/refpages/source/vkCmdPushConstants.html

The subsequent parameter-linkage extension uses the actual prepared compiler
interfaces rather than rejecting all PARAMs. It reuses the GPU planner's pure
cross-stage validator and checks actual sparse locations and unique component
counts, including builtins, against the physical device before image/buffer/
pipeline creation. Interpolation decorations remain actual compiler output;
no replacement shader, larger resource cap or guest-memory authority is added.
Vulkan interface limits follow the primary specification:
https://docs.vulkan.org/spec/latest/chapters/interfaces.html

